 :context
 "kotoba-lang/industry's registry entry for ISIC 0146 ('Raising of poultry') sat at
  :maturity :spec with no repository. Verified against a fresh, independent clone of
  kotoba-lang/industry before any work began (per this fleet's ID/name-mismatch
  caution -- two prior agents in this rollout mislabeled their assigned ISIC class).
  No prior cloud-itonami-isic-0146 repository existed (404 confirmed via gh api).
  Poultry-raising spans flock count/weight/mortality/egg-production record-keeping,
  veterinary appointment coordination, animal health/biosecurity concern escalation
  (e.g. suspected HPAI), and feed/veterinary-supply/biosecurity-equipment
  procurement. CRITICAL exclusions: direct animal handling, veterinary treatment
  decisions, and culling/depopulation decisions remain the exclusive authority of
  the farm operator/veterinarian."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct animal handling (farm operator's exclusive authority)"
  "veterinary treatment decisions (veterinarian/farm operator authority)"
  "culling or depopulation decisions (economic and ethical authority remains human)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0146 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Operation, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-0145 module-for-module, adapted
  to poultry/broiler-layer domain vocabulary):
  - Governor (PoultryFarmOperationsGovernor): 5 hard checks (facility-not-registered,
    no-execution, treatment-or-culling-blocked, op-not-allowed, flock-count-invalid)
    + 3 escalation gates (always-escalate health/biosecurity concern e.g. HPAI,
    cost-threshold supply orders, low confidence < 0.7)
  - Facts: supply categories with cost thresholds (feed/veterinary-supply/
    biosecurity-equipment), poultry breeds (broiler: Cobb 500/Ross 308; layer:
    White Leghorn/ISA Brown), biosecurity/notifiable-disease vocabulary (HPAI,
    Newcastle Disease, Infectious Bronchitis, Infectious Bursal Disease)
  - Registry: independent pure predicates (cost-exceeds-threshold?,
    flock-count-non-positive?, confidence-below-floor?)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (registered-facility lookup)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + MockAdvisor (4 ops)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate
  - Operation: composes advisor -> governor -> phase-gate (langgraph-clj wiring
    deferred, matching 0145's own stub)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main
  - Operations: log-flock-record, schedule-veterinary-visit,
    flag-animal-health-concern, order-supplies (closed allowlist, :effect :propose)
  - Tests: 32 tests / 103 assertions (facts, governor, phase, registry, store), all
    green -- one extra facts_test deftest vs. 0145 for poultry-specific broiler/layer
    :flock-type classification
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/business-model/operator-guide describe the real API (poultryops.operation's
    run-operation/build functions and :commit/:escalate/:hold dispositions)"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Poultry-raising (0146) now genuinely implemented and fully tested"
   "Scope boundaries (animal handling, treatment, culling/depopulation) hardcoded in
    governor checks, not just asserted in prose"
   "Animal-welfare/biosecurity escalation (flag-animal-health-concern always human,
    e.g. suspected HPAI) is a core design invariant"
   "Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["Real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up (in-memory for now)"
   "langgraph-clj StateGraph wiring (real interrupt-before/checkpoint resume) is
    deferred scaffolding, matching 0145's own stub status"]}

